{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"questions\":[\"Does “must be present in order to give rise to” state only a necessary threshold, or is the sentence intended to specify a sufficient trigger? On the necessary-only reading, the three facts can establish the threshold but cannot establish that a licensing obligation arises.\",\"Can the missing Circular or incorporated Ordinance resolve the tension between the express “at least one” threshold and the surrounding discussion of carrying on a business? Their contents are not supplied.\"],\"readings\":[{\"assumptions\":[\"This predicate concerns the selected applicability condition, not whole-law compliance or licence possession.\",\"Case-dependent input classifications and incorporated authority remain external to the encoded predicate.\",\"The declared input vocabulary is supplied for this controlled comparison; its adequacy as a legal abstraction remains unverified.\",\"“At least one” applies to all three listed factors; the final “and” closes the enumeration rather than imposing conjunction.\",\"For this antecedent experiment, satisfaction means meeting the stated one-or-more threshold. Treating that threshold as a sufficient licensing trigger requires an additional interpretive assumption.\"],\"citations\":[{\"quote\":\"at least one of which must be present\",\"unit_id\":\"daa1876316641.u38.27681\"},{\"quote\":\"firstly, the services provided by the family office constitute one or more regulated activity as defined under the Ordinance; secondly, the family office is carrying on a business in the provision of such services; and thirdly, the business is carried on in Hong Kong.\",\"unit_id\":\"daa1876316641.u38.27681\"}],\"distinction\":\"The explicit quantifier yields inclusive disjunction: any one, any two, or all three factors satisfy the antecedent. This is the preferred local textual reading, although “must” does not independently establish sufficiency.\",\"family\":\"